  "last_amend_reason": "ESC-029 grant registered. Adds amendment class esc-029-status-correction to .swarm-loop/amend-classes.json: tickets.json `status` FIELD ONLY, and only to correct a status that is demonstrably false -- a ticket recorded closed whose own defect still reproduces on the current tree, with the reproducing measurement recorded at each use. It is explicitly NOT permission to close tickets; a status edit toward closed is outside the class. Authorized by Hank 2026-09-06 ('if there's anything else that you need overridden, let me know right now'). The classes file is itself a protected path, so registering a grant in it IS an amendment and this is that record. STRUCTURAL PROOF: the only difference in the whole document is one added top-level key, esc-029-status-correction; esc-028-verify-fields is byte-identical, verified against HEAD's blob. No other protected path moved -- all 18 manifest hashes were re-derived and matched before this edit. A second class, esc-030-acceptance-graders, was deliberately NOT registered: it named kind 'frozen-path-amendment', which AMEND_CLASS_KINDS does not contain, so it would have been dropped as UNUSABLE and would have advertised an authority the tool cannot evaluate."
